.TH PATH-AUDIT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
path-audit \- report pathnames exceeding configurable byte thresholds
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B path-audit
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " DIRECTORY"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path-audit
scans directory entries and prints those with a basename component or
full pathname longer than the selected byte thresholds. It does not
rename or otherwise modify files and does not follow symbolic links.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--component-limit " N
Maximum accepted component byte length (default 240).
.TP
.BI "--path-limit " N
Maximum accepted pathname byte length (default 1024).
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Skip entries on filesystems other than that of the scan root.
.TP
.B --null
Print four NUL-terminated fields: REASON, COMPONENT_BYTES, PATH_BYTES, PATH.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Display usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B path-audit /srv/data
Apply default audit thresholds.
.TP
.B path-audit --component-limit 200 --path-limit 900 /home
Apply custom thresholds.
.SH OUTPUT
In text mode the report includes REASON (component, path or both), byte
counts and path, followed by the number of findings and errors. Control
characters in names are escaped. With --null all fields use NUL delimiters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 scan completed; 1 filesystem failure; 2 invalid arguments.
.SH NOTES
Limits are configurable audit values, not assertions about operating-system
NAME_MAX or PATH_MAX. The reported path includes the argument spelling;
relative and absolute roots may yield different path lengths.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR stat (1)
